course: dictionary
lesson: 2018
title: Confederacy: groups joined together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A confederacy is a group of states, tribes or people who join together for a shared purpose, such as defence, but each keeps much of its own power. The context gives you this meaning. «Five, later six, nations, including the Mohawk and Seneca, formed the Haudenosaunee Confederacy, a league of peace» shows several nations forming one group.
explain: Look for clues in «The Haudenosaunee Confederacy united the Mohawk, Oneida, Onondaga, Cayuga and Seneca.» The word united tells you the nations joined up, and the list shows who was in the group. Ask yourself: did they become one country with one ruler, or did each keep its own say? The text says clan mothers chose chiefs, so each nation kept its own ways.
explain: A capital letter is also a clue. «The Confederacy» with a capital C is a name in American history, for the group of southern states that broke away in 1861. A small c, as in «a confederacy», is a general word for any group joined for a shared purpose.
fact: A confederacy is a group joined together for a shared purpose, while each member keeps much of its own power.
fact: The Haudenosaunee Confederacy joined the Mohawk, Oneida, Onondaga, Cayuga and Seneca, later the Tuscarora, in a lasting alliance.
fact: «The Confederacy» was the group of eleven southern US states that broke away in 1861 to keep slavery and fought the North in the American Civil War.
fact: The Confederacy lost the war in 1865, and slavery was ended.
fact: A confederacy can also be a secret group that plans something together, especially something wrong; this is a formal meaning.
exercise: «Five, later six, nations, including the Mohawk and Seneca, formed the Haudenosaunee Confederacy, a league of peace.» What kind of group is a confederacy here? | A school sports team | A single nation ruled by one king | A hidden shop | *A group of nations joined together for peace
exercise: In history, which war did the Confederacy fight against the North? | The Hundred Years War | *The American Civil War | The Second World War | The Wars of the Roses
exercise: In «The Haudenosaunee Confederacy united the Mohawk, Oneida, Onondaga, Cayuga and Seneca», which word shows the nations joined up? | *united | Oneida | Mohawk | Cayuga
test: «The Confederacy broke away in 1861 to keep slavery.» What does broke away mean here? | Ran a race very fast | *Separated from the rest, leaving the group | Went out to play | Smashed a window
test: Which meaning fits a secret group that plans something together, especially something wrong? | A kind of cake baked for a party | *A group that meets in secret to plan something, often wrong | A sort of team sport played outdoors | A group of states that share a flag
exam: Mia says the Confederacy and a confederacy mean exactly the same. What is the best answer? | Yes, the capital letter is just for decoration | *No: the capital C names the southern US states that broke away in 1861, while a small c is any group joined for a shared purpose | No, a confederacy is always a sports team | Yes, both are a secret group that plans wrong things
